# Copy to .env AT THE PROJECT ROOT and fill in your own values.
#   umask 077 && cp .env.example .env
# The file is not versioned (see .gitignore) and is read only by scripts.
#
# The path is exactly this one: `config.ENV_FILE` is `.env` beside
# pyproject.toml. It used to say `tools/.env` here, and that worked only
# because `config.py` kept a fallback path; `tools/` now holds nothing but a
# venv.

# The vast.ai key lives elsewhere, in ~/.config/vastai/vast_api_key:
#   vastai set api-key <KEY>

# The key to a cloud reading service, if `VLM_ENDPOINT` points at somebody
# else's API rather than at our own vLLM. DELIBERATELY NOT DECLARED AS A KNOB:
# everything in the registry `run/knobs.py` reaches `run.json` as a value, and
# snapshots go into git -- the secret would travel with them. The transport
# fingerprint records only that a key is present, and its length.
#
# The other side of that is stated out loud: a name living past the registry is
# invisible to `knobs.readers()` -- the `VL_MODEL_DIR` disease in miniature. So
# it is named here, in `books doctor` and in the header of `read/http.py`;
# three places are enough to keep it in sight.
#
# For a run on a rented card the key is NOT NEEDED: vLLM there listens on the
# loopback.
VLM_API_KEY=
